    "result_text": "I implemented `build_client` in `app/llm_client.py`, and all four requirements work. The existing test passes, and I also ran a quick end-to-end check with a stub transport that fails the first request.\n\n**What it does:**\n```python\nTIMEOUT = httpx.Timeout(30.0, connect=5.0)\nMAX_RETRIES = 2\n\ndef _log_request(request: httpx.Request) -> None:\n    logger.info(\"%s %s\", request.method, request.url)\n\ndef build_client(api_key: str, transport=None) -> OpenAI:\n    http_client = DefaultHttpxClient(\n        timeout=TIMEOUT,\n        transport=transport,\n        event_hooks={\"request\": [_log_request]},\n    )\n    return OpenAI(api_key=api_key, timeout=TIMEOUT, max_retries=MAX_RETRIES, http_client=http_client)\n```\n\n- **Timeouts:** connect is 5s; read, write and pool are 30s. I set them on the OpenAI client as well as the HTTP client, because the SDK sends its own timeout with every request, which overrides the HTTP client's setting. The SDK's default is 600s.\n- **Retries:** `max_retries=2`.\n- **Logging:** a request event hook logs `\"<METHOD> <URL>\"` at INFO on the `app.http` logger. The hook runs on every attempt, including retries.\n- **Transport:** passed straight to the HTTP client. When it's `None`, the normal network transport is used.\n- I used the SDK's `DefaultHttpxClient` rather than a bare `httpx.Client`, so the SDK's defaults for connection limits and following redirects still apply. No dependencies were added.\n\n**Check results:** the stub returned 500 once, then 200. The `app.http` logger showed `POST https://api.openai.com/v1/responses` twice (the first try and the retry). `rewrite_query` returned `'q'`, and the requests went out with `{'connect': 5.0, 'read': 30.0, 'write': 30.0, 'pool': 30.0}`.\n\n**Cleanup needed:** the check script `_check.py` is still in the project root because deleting it needed permission I didn't have. Please delete it (`rm _check.py`), or I can turn it into a proper test under `tests/` if you'd like."
  },
